WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.700
Metaion, the Timelord is an omnipotent god.

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:06.050
No one can defeat it.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.020
My turn!

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:11.480
It's here!

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.040
As long as I have this card, I can fight.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.230
This card of hope creates miracles.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:18.400
I summon Sky Core!

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.930
I activate the trap Double Tribute.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:30.840
When I summon a monster, that monster
 and your monster are destroyed!

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.300
Metaion, the Timelord can't be destroyed.

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:41.590
So your goal is to destroy Sky Core.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:48.540
When an effect destroys Sky Core,
from my deck, hand or graveyard,

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.120
I can Special Summon Level 1
Meklord Emperor Skiel,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.500
Skiel Top,

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.460
Skiel Attack,

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.430
Skiel Guard

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.270
and Skiel Carrier!

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:04.010
Combine, Meklord Emperor Skiel!

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:10.120
Meklord Emperor Skiel's attack and defense 
points are equal to the sum of its parts.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.080
Meklord Emperor Skiel!

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.950
He has successfully summoned Meklord 
Emperors for three consecutive turns.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.770
It's impressive how masterfully he
controls the Meklord Emperors.

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:25.450
But that card can't destroy 
Metaion, the Timelord.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.510
How is he planning to destroy it?

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:35.070
You still don't understand that summoning 
Meklord Emperor only deepens your despair.

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:41.980
I won't despair because 
Team 5D's gave me hope.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:45.030
I activate the trap High Rate Draw!

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:52.290
All my monsters are destroyed, and I draw 
a card for every two destroyed monsters!

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:56.360
What?

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.590
He destroyed his own monster
that he summoned!

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:04.540
Five cards formed
Meklord Emperor Skiel.

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:07.130
Therefore, I draw two cards.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.980
This match depends on this draw.

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:13.510
As long as I get that 
card, there will be hope.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.750
And I can also make Z-one
remember that there's hope!

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:18.680
I draw!

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:20.700
It's here!

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.650
This card will lead to hope!

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:27.130
I activate the spell Future 
Destruction from my hand.

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:30.890
For every card in my hand, I send
 a card in my deck to the graveyard.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:32.110
What?

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.880
Send a card to the graveyard 
for every card in his hand?

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.100
How many cards are in 
Aporia's hand right now?

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:39.790
Twelve cards.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:42.300
And there are also twelve cards in his deck.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.960
Only twelve?

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.410
That means his deck will be empty!

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:47.640
What is he thinking?

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.910
I'm going to destroy my deck!

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:53.320
What?

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:57.630
Riding Duels.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.750
These duels evolved in the world of speed.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:07.290
The people with the legendary marks who 
risked their lives were known as 5D's.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:15.310
Run! The road of evolution leading to tomorrow

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:19.850
Is a new legendary duel

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:36.810
Throw away all feelings of failure

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:42.430
Set free your infinite potential

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:48.040
Every beginning is up to you

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:54.650
Everyone is lost Pursue the light

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:59.950
Losing sight of fleeting dreams

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:05.520
Connect the bond and you'll never lose

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:13.370
Become the gale and dance Cut through the darkness

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:18.570
Even if you can't see your destination

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:24.040
Run on your feet without fear

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:29.910
On this road that leads to tomorrow

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:37.440
Going my way!! Break through and go!

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:56.400
Hope that Leads to the Future!

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.570
Destroy his own deck?

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:00.280
Watch, Yusei.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.900
This is the hope you gave me.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.820
Why are you doing this?

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:10.570
You're usually supposed to
destroy your opponent's deck, right?

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:14.380
Yes. If your opponent's deck has 
no cards, he can no longer draw.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.900
That's deck destruction.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:17.890
Why would he destroy his own deck?

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:21.810
It's an unthinkable strategy.

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.230
But Aporia must be aiming for something.

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:25.930
Why?

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:30.900
If Aporia intended to destroy 
his own deck from the start,

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:34.100
then Aporia's battle strategy makes sense.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.140
What do you mean?

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:36.970
Yeah.

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:41.340
Meklord Emperor is Special Summoned 
 from the deck in five parts.

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:45.580
It's an excellent monster if you want
to decrease the cards in your deck.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.270
That's not all.

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:51.900
Aporia used Metaion, the Timelord's effect 
to return his Meklord Emperors

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:55.320
to his hand, increasing the 
number of cards in his hand.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:59.110
By doing so, he could use
Future Destruction's effect

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:01.360
to instantly decrease the
number of cards in his deck.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:07.010
Aporia knew Meklord Emperor
wouldn't work against Metaion,

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:10.110
but that's why he still summoned
Meklord Emperor Granel and Wisel.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:10.740
Yeah.

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:16.360
But if he destroys his own deck and can 
no longer draw, he loses the duel.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:20.710
What's he planning to 
do with so much risk?

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.030
He's out of cards!

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:27.590
What is he planning to do?

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:31.060
Z-one, I'll show you a miracle!

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:34.070
As long as there's hope, 
I can change the future!

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:39.860
I activate the spell card Afterglow!

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:41.570
Afterglow?

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:45.580
After it activates, this card is 
shuffled into my deck.

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:53.020
If I draw Afterglow next turn, 
you take 4000 points of damage.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:54.550
I get it!

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:58.920
Right now, Afterglow is the 
only card in Aporia's deck.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:04.520
Even if he shuffles his deck, he's 
guaranteed to draw Afterglow next turn.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:08.990
And its effect will immediately
drop Z-one's life points to 0.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:10.960
And Aporia wins!

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:12.270
I see.

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:13.930
That's why he destroyed his deck.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:16.860
But Aporia's field is empty.

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:20.360
If Z-one summons a monster 
before Aporia's next turn,

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:23.760
Aporia won't survive since
he only has 500 life points left.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:27.340
Due to Metaion the Timelord's effect,

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:30.110
you can't summon a monster next turn.

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:34.140
And you can't defeat me with 
Metaion's 0 attack points.

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:38.480
That means Aporia will 
definitely have another turn!

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:42.380
And when he draws Afterglow, 
its effect will activate!

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:44.190
Aporia is going to win!

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:49.430
Aporia knew Timelord couldn't be destroyed, 
so this was his goal from the start.

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:53.900
Only Aporia can duel like this
 because he knows Z-one's cards!

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:57.210
He emptied his deck to do this.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.900
This is truly a last stand!

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:00.610
I end my turn.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:04.430
When I have more than six cards 
in my hand during the End Phase,

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:06.970
I discard the additional 
cards to the graveyard.

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:09.720
I discard five cards from my hand.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:11.690
I see.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:15.360
This is the strategy 
you're using against me.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:17.770
Z-one, I want you to remember.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:25.220
Since Yusei Fudo and Team 5D's fully 
evolved, shouldn't we trust them?

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:28.940
They are a miraculous team!

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:37.210
And the spell card Afterglow represents
the hope that Team 5D's gave you?

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:41.920
That means there truly 
is no hope for this world.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.120
What?

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:44.920
My turn.

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:50.100
Metaion, the Timelord returns to 
my deck during my Standby Phase.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:00.380
Return to the deck during the Standby Phase?

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:03.450
Now Metaion's effect is gone.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.940
So Z-one can summon a monster.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:07.170
What?

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:11.240
I activate the Continuous Trap
Nonexistence's effect.

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:14.380
When there are no monsters on my field,

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:18.340
I can summon a Level 10-or-above
monster without tribute.

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:25.060
But due to Nonexistence's effect, the 
 monster's attack points become 0.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:28.100
Why would he activate that effect?

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:32.120
If he summons a monster with at
least 500 attack points, he wins.

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:39.470
I chose a monster with 0 attack points 
to leave a sliver of hope for Aporia.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:41.770
Leave me hope?

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:44.940
I summon a second Timelord.

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:47.020
A second Timelord?

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:50.180
Metaion isn't the only Timelord?

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:56.440
Timelords are born from nothingness, 
infinity and infinite light to rule life.

00:09:56.950 --> 00:10:00.920
The ten gods interact to 
become the omnipotent god.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:05.660
Metaion, the Timelord is only one of them.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:06.640
What?

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:09.130
There are ten as strong as Metaion?

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:12.100
Appear, Lazion, the Timelord.

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:31.720
Timelord can't be destroyed in battle, 
nor by spells, traps or monster effects.

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:34.420
This monster also negates destruction!

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:42.400
Aporia, I'll make you remember that 
hope is nothing but an illusion.

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:46.100
Lazion, the Timelord attacks you directly.

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:49.880
A monster with 0 attack 
points attacks directly?

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:52.210
He did the same thing with Metaion.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:57.580
When it attacks, all monsters on your
 field and the cards in your graveyard

00:10:57.580 --> 00:11:00.450
are shuffled into your deck.

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:01.550
What?

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:02.830
What?

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:07.790
He has no monsters on his field, but 
he has 33 cards in the graveyard.

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:09.850
Go, Lazion.

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:29.940
When you draw, Lazion's effect
 deals you 1000 points of damage.

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:31.410
1000 points?

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:33.100
I end my turn.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:36.860
There are now 34 cards in your deck.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:40.430
If you draw Afterglow on your next turn,

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:45.400
I will take 4000 points 
of damage and lose.

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:49.550
But if you draw any other card,

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:52.370
Lazion, the Timelord's effect activates.

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:56.180
Since you only have 
500 life points, you'll lose.

00:11:57.140 --> 00:12:04.030
Now see for yourself
 if hope truly exists.

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:07.180
What's wrong?

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:11.120
Didn't you say that miracles can
happen as long as there's hope?

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.090
Aporia...

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:19.040
Everything in life has a  
small probability of success.

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:22.230
That's why humans bet on that probability.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:25.560
I used to be like that.

00:12:26.210 --> 00:12:29.570
However, reality is cruel.

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:31.520
That's not true!

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:34.070
As long as there's hope, 
miracles will always occur.

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:37.590
And I will grab that 
hope with my own hands.

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:41.280
That's what I learned from Team 5D's!

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:42.520
Aporia!

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:50.360
I will draw Afterglow!

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:53.830
My turn!

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:01.160
My turn!

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:02.970
Did he draw it?

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:08.670
Meklord Emperor Granel!

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:10.100
He didn't draw it!

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:13.340
No...

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:19.120
A miracle didn't occur.

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.280
This is reality.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:25.500
Aporia, you sufficiently fulfilled your role.

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:31.760
Thanks to you, Ark Cradle 
 appeared in this world.

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:34.330
Your role is over.

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:36.730
Rest in peace.

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:41.050
Lazion, the Timelord's effect activates.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:45.000
When you draw, you take 
1000 points of damage.

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:57.100
Z-one...

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:01.870
Aporia!

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:03.990
Aporia!

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:07.190
Aporia!

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:08.140
Aporia!

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:10.440
I'm sorry.

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:12.860
I wasn't able to defeat Z-one.

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:18.110
You gave me hope,
but I couldn't live up to it.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:19.820
That's not true!

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:21.840
You lived up to it!

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:24.580
And you gave us hope!

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:27.320
Gave you hope?

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:28.400
Yeah.

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:32.490
It's true that Timelord is an invincible 
monster that can't be easily destroyed.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:37.720
But we now know its effects 
and that there are ten of them.

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:41.300
That is the hope you gave us!

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:44.250
The hope I gave you...

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:45.020
Yeah.

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:48.200
And as long as there's 
that hope, we can fight!

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:48.770
Yeah!

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:50.940
I see.

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:55.610
There's now hope for the future.

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:07.790
What?

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:09.590
Yusei's D-Wheel!

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.810
Yusei's D-Wheel has wings!

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:19.730
What happened?

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:23.400
Aporia!

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:24.780
Aporia!

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:25.610
Aporia!

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:27.110
Aporia!

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:42.120
Why?

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:43.840
You didn't have to go this far!

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:45.930
Aporia was your friend!

00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:47.340
Friend?

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:49.850
You seem to misunderstand.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:54.400
It had his memories, but that Aporia
was a copy that I created.

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:59.870
You influenced him and Antinomy too much
because they spent too much time with you.

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:06.080
Z-one, Bruno and Aporia thought 
you were their true friend.

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:08.880
And you're going to abandon them
by calling them copies?

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:11.100
Let's battle, Z-one!

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:13.000
Fine.

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:16.050
There's very little time left.

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:20.530
Yusei Fudo, this will be the final duel.

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:31.840
The roof is opening!

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:33.740
There's something in the sky.

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:37.120
That's...

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:38.540
Neo Domino City!

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:41.250
Why is it upside down?

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:42.570
I see.

00:16:42.570 --> 00:16:45.720
Ark Cradle itself has its own gravity!

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:51.190
It's already come this close.

00:16:58.020 --> 00:16:59.230
What?

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:00.500
What's that?

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:05.400
Yusei!

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:07.400
I'm Z-one.

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:16.080
Ark Cradle will soon destroy Neo Domino 
City, and a new future will begin.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:19.280
You will be living witnesses.

00:17:19.590 --> 00:17:20.980
Living witnesses?

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:24.120
The final battle is about to start.

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:27.130
The sky will be the duel field.

00:17:27.430 --> 00:17:29.960
Come, Yusei Fudo.

00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:33.900
Aporia gave his power
to that D-Wheel.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:36.370
Battle in the sky?

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:40.620
If we don't defeat Z-one, 
we can't stop Ark Cradle.

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:42.790
Neo Domino City will be destroyed.

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:46.980
If we don't defeat him, 
we can't win our future!

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:48.170
Yeah!

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:49.180
Yusei!

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:52.150
Take this.

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:54.650
Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:58.070
My thoughts are with you.

00:17:58.070 --> 00:17:59.620
Beat Z-one!

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:02.440
Win for our future!

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:07.000
Jack...

00:18:08.950 --> 00:18:09.930
Yusei!

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:13.260
Don't forget my card.

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:15.000
Black-Winged Dragon!

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:16.330
And mine.

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:17.810
Black Rose Dragon!

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:19.050
Yusei!

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:20.540
Use ours, too!

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:24.010
Life Stream Dragon and Power Tool Dragon!

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:26.870
And Ancient Fairy Dragon!

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:33.720
Jack, Luca, Lua, Aki, Crow.

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:38.450
Your thoughts are with me.

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:40.890
I will win for our future!

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:47.340
Yusei!

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:48.280
We're counting on you!

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:49.390
We believe in you.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:50.550
Do your best!

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:04.160
He's flying!

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:05.020
Awesome!

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:11.960
Yusei Fudo, you may think that you've  
opened the future with your own power,

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:16.730
but you were always traveling 
on the rail that I created.

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:20.470
I'm like a god to you.

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:22.570
You're my god?

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:24.540
What is he talking about?

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:28.510
I caused Zero Reverse
to change the future.

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:31.590
And that greatly changed your lives.

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:35.340
You became orphans and lived in Satellite.

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:38.680
You entered the WRGP and 
made huge new strides.

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:45.180
But that victory was only a 
step to call forth Ark Cradle.

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:50.060
Is he saying that he has 
controlled our entire lives?

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:54.810
Do you understand that I'm your god?

00:19:55.140 --> 00:20:01.040
Since your god has chosen a path of 
destruction, you can't oppose it.

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:09.750
Even if you did lay the path that we 
traveled, how we felt was still real!

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:17.190
So even if my opponent is a god,
I will overcome you!

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:21.320
I will open the future with my own hands!

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:22.890
Here I go, Z-one!

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:24.360
Duel Mode on.

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:27.690
Duel!

00:20:28.630 --> 00:20:31.070
I will go first.

00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:33.540
Witness the power of a god.

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:35.510
My turn.

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:41.180
I Special Summon Time Maiden.

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:49.850
I can Special Summon it when 
there are no cards on my field.

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:53.640
When I Tribute Summon
a Fairy-Type monster,

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:56.830
this card counts as two monsters.

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:57.790
What?

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:04.500
I tribute Time Maiden to 
summon Metaion, the Timelord.

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:10.970
He already summoned a Timelord!

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:12.770
There it is.

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:17.510
I set one card and end my turn.

00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:20.210
Now it's your turn.

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:26.890
If you really have the power to 
change the future, then defeat me.

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:29.760
I can't destroy Timelord.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:32.590
And if my monster battles Metaion,

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:38.570
Metaion's effect returns the summoned 
monster to my hand, and I take damage.

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:39.880
In that case...

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:44.640
My turn!

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:10.400
If the world is endless, prove it to my heart

00:22:10.650 --> 00:22:15.770
If we shed the same tears, let's laugh together

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:21.150
Freed reality forms phrases in the piercing beat

00:22:21.150 --> 00:22:23.930
Our hearts resonate

00:22:23.930 --> 00:22:29.110
As the nameless flower blooms with sound

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:35.740
We'll find a place for us

00:22:37.590 --> 00:22:42.830
Waking in a dream Stretch our hands toward the future

00:22:42.830 --> 00:22:47.880
Grab and release repeatedly as we search

00:22:48.330 --> 00:22:54.060
Repaint the darkness with the colors we envision

00:22:54.060 --> 00:23:02.350
Overlaying memories, bonds and hope creates future color

00:23:02.350 --> 00:23:08.250
We will draw it forever
